WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
One Vera CPU replaces the dual CPU Bluefield 4, giving context memory servers a cheaper board. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres Episode 29. Intel's waver fight over foreign fab robots comes next, then a former Navy site in San Diego and Canada's Ontario notice, and the closes on the horizon. NVIDIA put the Bluefield 4 STX server on the floor at OCP 2026, and served the home walk the board partners had been requesting. The earlier card gave each processor

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:36.540
S.O.K.A.M. and carried 4 Connect X9 Supernix, and it sat closer to a dual-socket server

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.000
than to a Bluefield 1 or Bluefield 3.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:45.040
This card is much smaller with high-density connectors for PCI Express and the system links,

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.760
and the package is a high-end server CPU rather than an embedded DPU core.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:55.200
S.O.K.A.M leaves the top of the package clear for a heat sink or a liquid cooling block,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.620
stock, and an M.2 slot is there for what is usually the operating system drive.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:07.140
A soldered processor and LPDDR5X instead of DDR5 dim slots, keep the board about the size

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:14.240
of an Intel DMR 16 channel socket or a 16 channel AMD EPYC Venice platform, and the layout

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.540
is meant to go together on an automatic line.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:22.620
No Connect X9 Supernix showed up on the board's photograph at the booths, and NAND prices have

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.780
been rising meaningfully over the past year.

00:01:25.744 --> 00:01:33.404
Quantinium reported 99.995% logical memory fidelity on Helios, about 5 failures in a million

00:01:33.404 --> 00:01:33.864
cycles.

00:01:34.564 --> 00:01:39.164
Chief Executive Rajeeb Hazara told the Wall Street Journal this de-risks the industry.

00:01:39.884 --> 00:01:43.504
HPC Wire says the Helios results strengthens the path to Apollo.

00:01:44.164 --> 00:01:46.684
The fault-tolerant machine Quantinium has planned.

00:01:48.684 --> 00:01:54.564
Models early benchmarks, which ARM highlighted, put Nvidia's Vera CPU add up to twice the

00:01:54.564 --> 00:01:58.264
throughput of comparable X86 systems when concurrency is heavy.

00:01:58.864 --> 00:02:04.364
Jupiter, Europe's first Exascale Supercomputer, is where Nvidia just logged a record quantum

00:02:04.364 --> 00:02:04.984
simulation.

00:02:05.604 --> 00:02:10.884
The run validated magic state cultivation, a fault tolerant method that needs 90% fewer

00:02:10.884 --> 00:02:12.404
qubits than earlier approaches.

00:02:14.347 --> 00:02:19.327
Great Skies, superconducting neural network chip, which borrows techniques from quantum

00:02:19.327 --> 00:02:23.307
computers, past a battery of tests on data from a fusion reactor.

00:02:24.107 --> 00:02:29.747
Brookhaven National Laboratory, Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory, and the D3ID National

00:02:29.747 --> 00:02:35.207
Fusion Facility are in the partnership under what HPC wire ties to the Genesis mission.

00:02:35.927 --> 00:02:37.767
These chips are not conventional silicon.

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:44.809
Manchester Financial Group is exploring a 400-megawatt data center at the former

00:02:44.809 --> 00:02:50.849
Navy, NAV-war headquarters in San Diego, California. Data Center Dynamics frames that as a site

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:57.297
being eyed, not a campus that is energized. Canada has put out an advanced procurement

00:02:57.297 --> 00:03:03.597
notice for a data center in Ontario. The estimate runs from 1.5 billion to 1.85 billion

00:03:03.597 --> 00:03:07.317
Canadian dollars, and a notice is not assigned build contract.

00:03:08.597 --> 00:03:15.557
Dylan Patel of semi-analysis said there is no correction, 195 MW go up in 2027 in the

00:03:15.557 --> 00:03:15.877
model.

00:03:16.577 --> 00:03:20.677
Crusoe's figures sit a bit higher, and Patel said the model follows what will actually

00:03:20.677 --> 00:03:21.237
be built.

00:03:21.757 --> 00:03:27.717
That capacity is under construction now, some of it goes live in 2027, and partial construction

00:03:27.717 --> 00:03:29.277
of sites is already in the count.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:35.830
Amazon is linked to a possible front-of-the-meter deal at a large AI data center it is building

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:40.530
in Texas, and data center knowledge says the company is still exploring, not committed.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:45.370
In that framing, the plant feeds the grid instead of reserving power for one campus.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:50.810
Behind the meter generation serves a single facility, and a grid interactive plant still

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.770
exists first to support the data center.

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:58.490
Backing a grid serving plant is capital intensive, and most operators are still on utility

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:03.030
partnerships, long-term power buys, storage and behind-the-meter generation.

00:04:04.853 --> 00:04:11.073
Intel filed a waiver with the FCC on October 16th, made public Monday in the account Biggo

00:04:11.073 --> 00:04:12.593
Finance draws from Bloomberg.

00:04:13.153 --> 00:04:18.693
In July, the FCC put advanced robots made outside the United States on its covered list, next

00:04:18.693 --> 00:04:20.253
to Wi-Fi routers and drones.

00:04:20.813 --> 00:04:23.493
So those products cannot be sold into the US market.

00:04:24.093 --> 00:04:28.913
Machines already installed can stay, but their hardware, software, and firmware can no longer

00:04:28.913 --> 00:04:34.453
be updated. Intel's fabs move material on automated guided vehicles long-supplied by

00:04:34.453 --> 00:04:40.433
Marata machinery and Daifuku. There is no validated U.S. made alternative that meets Intel standards,

00:04:40.873 --> 00:04:46.033
and a full replacement would take years. Intel called continued operation critical to U.S.

00:04:46.173 --> 00:04:51.133
national security and said a disruption would immediately and negatively affect U.S. chip capacity,

00:04:51.613 --> 00:04:56.093
and it asked for a conditional waiver because it is unclear whether an upgrade would break the rule.

00:04:57.013 --> 00:05:02.833
TSMC, Micron, Global Foundry, Samsung Electronics, and Texas Instruments may need the same waiver,

00:05:03.313 --> 00:05:05.873
and there is no information that any of them has filed.

00:05:06.413 --> 00:05:09.093
The covered list has moved to whole categories of gear.

00:05:09.693 --> 00:05:14.373
Net gear received a license in April after the Defense Department found no national security

00:05:14.373 --> 00:05:14.713
threat.

00:05:15.253 --> 00:05:20.393
An AT&amp;T, Verizon, and a broadband association were allowed hardware upgrades on consumer

00:05:20.393 --> 00:05:21.533
Wi-Fi routers.

00:05:23.609 --> 00:05:29.449
Qualcomm won key claims against ARM in a four-year intellectual property fight, and EE times

00:05:29.449 --> 00:05:30.829
puts the damages at $2.

00:05:31.369 --> 00:05:36.209
The verdict protects Qualcomm's custom processors and puts financial pressure on ARM.

00:05:38.426 --> 00:05:45.946
ESD Alliance, a semi-technology coalition, reported electronic system design revenue of $5,710.8

00:05:45.946 --> 00:05:48.486
million in the second quarter of 2026.

00:05:48.486 --> 00:05:56.406
That is up 12.2% from $5,089.4 million in the same quarter of 2025, semiconductor

00:05:56.406 --> 00:05:57.566
digest reports.

00:05:58.668 --> 00:06:04.568
Handme semiconductor also today opened its U.S. subsidiary Handme USA as a step into the

00:06:04.568 --> 00:06:06.148
American semiconductor market.

00:06:06.708 --> 00:06:13.168
A Japanese research institute has a new quantum HPC system built around 540 NVIDIA GPUs,

00:06:13.568 --> 00:06:14.848
quantum zeitgeist reports.

00:06:14.848 --> 00:06:19.808
A Russian official has proposed citing data centers and disused coal mines so drone

00:06:19.808 --> 00:06:27.100
strikes are harder to land. Aurora at Argon kept 13.4 trillion dark matter particles

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:33.240
resident in each of two runs, and that residency is the place to take it apart. HPC Wire says

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:37.920
the Argon team used Aurora to finish two of the largest cosmological simulations yet,

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:44.600
each one across a region 28.6 billion light years wide. The code is HACC, and gravity

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:49.560
is the only force, so each particle is a tracer of density and velocity rather than a packet

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:59.240
of gas, stars, or radiation. Aurora has 10,624 nodes and 63,744 GPUs. Each run took

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:05.760
8,100 nodes and about 50,000 GPUs, and the simulations plus much of the analysis finished

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:11.040
in about four days. High capacity memory is the limit the team names, because trillions

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.200
of particles had to stay available as the calculation moved.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:16.640
The restart path is the other half.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.160
Aurora's DO storage took the checkpoints.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:23.520
The two simulations wrote more than 85 petabytes through DOS.

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:27.060
Mostly so an interruption can resume instead of starting over.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.660
About 8 petabytes were kept for the science.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:35.680
More than 85 against about 8 means the checkpoint stream is more than 10 times the analysis archive.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:39.460
Most of the bytes were the right to continue, not the sky itself.

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:45.760
The same HACC team had already used frontier for a hydrodynamic run that added gas, stars,

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:50.640
and other galaxy formation processes, and that was the largest hydrodynamic simulation

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:51.940
of the universe to date.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:57.040
Adding those fields multiplies the state per particle, which is why gravity alone is

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.040
what let Aurora hold the larger volume.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:04.080
When galaxy formation has to live in the same box as that largest scale density field,

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:09.200
the residence set and the checkpoint both grow, and the gravity only cut is no longer

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.200
the run the survey analysis requires.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:18.080
On the horizon, Continuum still dates Apollo, its planned fault tolerant machine to

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:18.840
2029.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.460
A larger, great sky fusion control chip is due for more testing next year.

